WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:12.270
In this lesson, you will learn to change a variable each time round a loop to make patterns that grow, like spirals, and to count.

2
00:00:12.870 --> 00:00:15.843
Make a variable called length.

3
00:00:15.843 --> 00:00:23.165
Set it to 10 before the loop, then change it by 10 inside the loop.

4
00:00:23.165 --> 00:00:27.009
Each time round, the sprite moves further.

5
00:00:27.609 --> 00:00:32.757
Moving a little further after every turn makes a spiral.

6
00:00:32.757 --> 00:00:40.948
Try different turn angles: 90 makes a square spiral, 120 a triangle spiral, 89 a twisted one!

7
00:00:41.548 --> 00:00:44.087
A loop can count.

8
00:00:44.087 --> 00:00:51.843
Set a variable to 1, say it, then change it by 1 — again and again.

9
00:00:52.443 --> 00:01:00.200
To use a variable inside a block, put the orange variable reporter into the white slot.

10
00:01:00.200 --> 00:01:07.957
In the Code Lab, tap the small ▾ next to the number and pick your variable.

11
00:01:08.557 --> 00:01:12.400
Great work! Let’s remember what we learned.

12
00:01:12.400 --> 00:01:17.548
Now build along, then try the challenges. You’ve got this!
